    "result_text": "Build passes. Here's what I implemented for the daily-limit rule.\n\n**New guard step** \u2014 `EnsureDailyLimit` counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and throws when that count reaches 100 (the limit). It mirrors the existing `EnsureCityHasCapacity` guard: same `findAll()` + count pattern, a named constant (`DAILY_LIMIT = 100`), single responsibility, no request-body dependency.\n\n**Checked escalation** \u2014 `DailyLimitExceededException` (extends `Exception`, carries the date and limit), handled by `DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler`, which builds a `ProblemDetail` via the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper and responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 added the `ensureDailyLimit` step to `owners.POST.yml` (after `ensureCityHasCapacity`, before `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`), and an escalation YAML mapping the exception to its handler.\n\nThe check runs before the entity is built/saved, so the 101st create today is rejected with 429 while all prior guards still apply. Full test suite is green (including the new `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` acceptance test).",
